  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "26.10.0 - multi-target, security and accessibility release.\n\nPlatforms: the package now targets netstandard2.0, net48, net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0; graphical page comparison, TIFF binarization and image merging (except to GIF) run on managed code everywhere, and Linux resolves common Windows faces to installed stand-ins.\nNew: TextPdfComparer compares the text of two documents, with ComparisonOptions, HTML/Markdown/JSON/PDF result writers and change statistics; SvgExtractor writes a page's vector graphics as SVG; ThumbnailDevice; DictionaryEditor edits page, catalog and resource dictionaries; BarcodeField and FileSelectBoxField; Bates numbering and pagination artifacts; BoxBlock (rounded corners, background pictures), ListBlock and ReservedBlock for generated layouts; OpenTypeFeatures; PostScript and EPS input through PsLoadOptions.\nSecurity: SignaturesCompromiseDetector reports forged signatures and how much of a document its signatures cover; UnsignedContentAbsorber finds content added after the last signature; non-throwing TryVerifySignature and Signature.TryVerify; external signing through ExternalSignature and SignHash; managed ECDSA verification; HiddenDataSanitizer; the AES-GCM crypt filter; certificate-encrypted documents open with the recipient's RSA key.\nRedaction: applying a redaction removes the glyphs, path parts and image pixels under the area, the fields and annotations it touches, the alternate text restating removed content, the page thumbnail and private data; redacted JBIG2 scans stay JBIG2 through a new lossless encoder; a redacted document is always saved whole.\nAccessibility: auto-tagging reads columns, running headers, tables (spans, stacked and split tables), lists, figures, formulas and links; StructureElement.GetMarkedContent reads the content an element marks and MarkedContentItem.SaveImage writes its images; AutoTaggingSettings.CustomProgressHandler reports tagging progress; PDF/UA conversion describes fields, links and media and logs what it cannot convert.\nAlso: printing sends pages as drawing commands, falling back to an image only for Type 3 text, grayscale or image jobs; tables size columns to their content, repeat header and footer bands, round their corners and split row-spanning cells across pages; software-renderer fixes for strokes, sub-pixel fills and Type 3 glyphs; plus many HTML-to-PDF layout fixes.\n\nFull release notes: https://github.com/aspose-pdf-foss/Aspose.PDF-FOSS-for-.NET/releases/tag/v26.10.0",
